# UNIT THEME ENRICHMENT — Creativity Techniques (UEM)

Run **before** `ct-unit-forge` writes student lessons. Output feeds both the
professor brief and the student slideshow main-idea list
([`STUDENT-SLIDESHOW-FORGE.mdc`](./STUDENT-SLIDESHOW-FORGE.mdc)).

## Goal

For each official unit **U1–U6**, produce an enrichment pack that:

1. Broadcasts the unit theme across **Athanor / DevIAC** (`project_slug=profield-creativity-techniques`, `knowledge_scope=field_prospection`) and related scholarly vaults  
2. Cross-checks **Profield** prospection (`~/src/profield/runs/creativity-techniques/20260909/`)  
3. Extracts **main ideas**, **connections**, **repeated referred works**, and **recurring authors**  
4. Summarises **≤ 6 main ideas** for the student slideshow  
5. Keeps the **full findings** on the professor-facing page (unpublished pedagogy tree)

## Ready-to-run discovery commands

```bash
# Vectors (smoke-tested live)
curl -s -X POST http://localhost:8100/vectors/search \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"query":"<unit theme>","project_slug":"profield-creativity-techniques","knowledge_scope":"field_prospection","n_results":12}'

# Optional MCP: search_knowledge with the same project_slug / knowledge_scope

# Cite only after Ahmes resolve (never paste vector snippets into lessons)
# ahmes query --cite "$DB:<node_id>" --style chicago-author-date
```

Cross-project broadcast (same theme, adjacent slugs — discovery only):

| Slug | Use |
| ---- | --- |
| `profield-creativity-techniques` | Primary domain |
| `profield-didactics` | How people learn / technique pedagogy (never substitute for domain cites) |
| `profield-digital-creativity` | Sibling craft context only when U5 (technology) needs a bridge |

## Pack layout (one directory per unit)

```text
creativity-techniques-pedagogy/forge/unit-enrichment/
  INDEX.md                 # run status for U1–U6
  _template/
    PROFESSOR.md           # full findings
    MAIN-IDEAS.yml         # ≤ 6 slides payloads
  U1-introduccion-creatividad/
    PROFESSOR.md
    MAIN-IDEAS.yml
    discovery-receipt.json # queries, timestamps, hit counts (no cite claims)
  …
```

### PROFESSOR.md (required sections)

1. Unit CONTENIDOS anchor (verbatim from guía)  
2. Discovery queries run (text + slug + date)  
3. Recurring authors (frequency across hits)  
4. Recurring works (titles / DOIs when known)  
5. Connection graph (who talks to whom — short prose or bullet edges)  
6. Candidate main ideas (draft > 6 allowed here)  
7. Cite-ready shortlist (Ahmes coat · node · page — or honest `[BIBLIO-GAP]`)  
8. Gaps / risks for teaching  
9. Proposed ≤ 6 slideshow ideas (final cut)

### MAIN-IDEAS.yml (student-bound)

```yaml
unit_id: U2
max_ideas: 6
ideas:
  - id: 1
    heading: "…"
    sentence: "…"
    chicago: null   # or "(Author Year, page)" when evaluator-safe
```

## Gate before lesson forge

| Check | Required |
| ----- | -------- |
| Enrichment pack exists for the unit | ✅ |
| MAIN-IDEAS.yml has 1–6 ideas | ✅ |
| PROFESSOR.md lists discovery queries | ✅ |
| Evidence matrix row updated in `grounding/` | ✅ (may be honest NONE / gap) |
| Student HTML contains no studio infra names | ✅ |

